---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — Try Convi"
  description="How Try Convi collects, uses, and protects your data."
>
  <article class="legal">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: 16 July 2026</p>

    <p>
      This Privacy Policy explains what information Try Convi ("we", "us")
      collects, how we use it, and the choices you have. By using{" "}
      <a href="https://tryconvi.com">tryconvi.com</a> you agree to this policy.
    </p>

    <h2>Information we collect</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Email address.</strong> If you sign up or make a purchase, we
        collect the email you provide so we can send you updates and verify your
        access to paid features.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Purchase records.</strong> When you buy Practice mode, our
        payment provider notifies us of the email associated with your purchase
        so we can unlock your access. We do not receive or store your card
        details.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Usage analytics.</strong> We use Cloudflare Web Analytics, which
        is privacy-first: it does not use cookies and does not track or identify
        individual visitors. It only gives us aggregate figures like page views,
        referring sites, countries, and site performance.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Local storage.</strong> After you unlock Practice mode, we store
        a small flag in your browser so you don't have to re-enter your email
        each visit. This stays on your device.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Technical data.</strong> We temporarily process IP addresses to
        rate-limit our forms and protect against abuse. These are not stored
        long-term or used to profile you.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How we use your information</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>To provide access to purchased features.</li>
      <li>To send you product updates and respond to your messages.</li>
      <li>To understand overall traffic and improve the site.</li>
      <li>To protect the service from abuse.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Payments</h2>
    <p>
      Purchases are processed by Gumroad, which acts as the merchant of record.
      Your payment information is handled entirely by Gumroad under their own
      privacy policy and terms. We never see your full card details.
    </p>

    <h2>Sharing</h2>
    <p>
      We do not sell your personal information. We share data only with the
      service providers that make Try Convi work — our payment processor
      (Gumroad), email provider (Resend), hosting and data infrastructure
      (Vercel, Upstash), and analytics (Cloudflare) — and only as needed to run
      the service.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      You can ask us to access or delete the personal data we hold about you at
      any time. Just email us and we'll take care of it.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy? Email{" "}
      <a href="mailto:hello@tryconvi.com">hello@tryconvi.com</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal {
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .legal h1 {
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  .legal .updated {
    color: var(--color-ink-soft);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .legal h2 {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    font-size: 1.25rem;
  }

  .legal a {
    color: var(--color-primary);
  }

  .legal li {
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }
</style>
